+## When `beforeSession` throws
+
+- `beforeSession` is called inside the orchestrator's `try` block, so a throw there reaches the same `catch`/`finally` as any other failure in the turn: the caller still receives the rejection, `onError` fires with that error, and `afterSession` runs. A deployer can assume no tools were run, no provider was called and no entry was committed — the turn was aborted before it began — so `afterSession` after a failed `beforeSession` sees the session as it stood on entry and cannot distinguish "never allocated" from "allocated and finished" ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L36)).
